  "family": "Pittosporaceae",
  "memo": "This tree is known for its striking, fragrant yellow flowers that bloom in clusters, providing a delightful scent to urban areas. Its dark green, glossy leaves create a lush canopy that offers ample shade. As it matures, the tree develops a slender, upright trunk with rough, grayish bark. It thrives in full sun and well-drained soils, making it a versatile choice for various landscapes. The flowers gradually turn from yellow to cream, adding a dynamic color display throughout the blooming season. This tree is relatively low-maintenance and can attract birds and pollinators, enhancing the biodiversity of urban spaces.",
