  "schoolyard_use_notes": "This tree produces fragrant, yellow flowers that can be used in lessons about pollination and plant reproduction. The flowers transition to a creamy white as they age, providing a visual example of plant aging and lifecycle. Its evergreen leaves stay on the tree year-round, making it useful for discussions about different leaf retention strategies. The tree's growth habit and size make it suitable for studying plant structure and habitat preferences. The seeds develop in woody pods, which can be used to explore seed dispersal methods.",
